[Tool Use]: Bash({'command': 'cat > /tmp/pr_review.json << 'ENDJSON'
{
  "commit_id": "641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1",
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "## Code review\n\nFound 6 issues. Checked for bugs and CLAUDE.md compliance.",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "app_utils.py",
      "line": 6,
      "start_line": 5,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "start_side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**CLAUDE.md violation: Hardcoded credentials**\n\nPasswords and host addresses must not be stored in source code. Anyone with read access to the repo gets these credentials.\n\nRule from [`CLAUDE.md`](https://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/CLAUDE.md#L7): _\"Never hardcode sensitive credentials (passwords, API keys, tokens) in source code. Use environment variables.\"_\n\nReplace with:\n```python\nPASSWORD = os.environ.get(\"DB_PASSWORD\")\nDB_HOST = os.environ.get(\"DB_HOST\")\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/app_utils.py#L4-L7"
    },
    {
      "path": "app_utils.py",
      "line": 10,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**CLAUDE.md violation: SQL injection via string concatenation**\n\n`username` is concatenated directly into the SQL string. An attacker can pass `' OR '1'='1` to bypass authentication, or `'; DROP TABLE users;--` to destroy data.\n\nRule from [`CLAUDE.md`](https://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/CLAUDE.md#L4): _\"Never use string concatenation or interpolation to construct SQL queries. Always use parameterized queries or an ORM.\"_\n\nUse a parameterized query instead:\n```python\nquery = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?\"\n# cursor.execute(query, (username,))\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/app_utils.py#L9-L11"
    },
    {
      "path": "app_utils.py",
      "line": 15,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**CLAUDE.md violation: Command injection via `os.system`**\n\n`user_input` is concatenated into a shell command without sanitization. An attacker can pass `; rm -rf /` to execute arbitrary commands on the server.\n\nRule from [`CLAUDE.md`](https://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/CLAUDE.md#L5): _\"Never pass unsanitized user input directly to system shells (e.g., `os.system`).\"_\n\nUse `subprocess.run` with a list of arguments (no shell interpolation):\n```python\nimport subprocess\nsubprocess.run([\"ls\", user_input], check=True)\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/app_utils.py#L13-L16"
    },
    {
      "path": "app_utils.py",
      "line": 20,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**CLAUDE.md violation: Insecure deserialization with `pickle` (RCE risk)**\n\n`pickle.load` executes arbitrary Python bytecode embedded in the file. A malicious pickle payload can achieve Remote Code Execution with no additional exploit needed.\n\nRule from [`CLAUDE.md`](https://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/CLAUDE.md#L6): _\"Do not use `pickle` for deserializing untrusted data due to RCE risks. Use `json` instead.\"_\n\nReplace with `json`:\n```python\nimport json\n\ndef load_data(file_path):\n    with open(file_path, \"r\") as f:\n        return json.load(f)\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/app_utils.py#L17-L21"
    },
    {
      "path": "app_utils.py",
      "line": 24,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**CLAUDE.md violation: Missing zero-division guard (guaranteed `ZeroDivisionError`)**\n\nThis function performs `x / y` with no check on `y`. The `__main__` block at line 51 calls `calculate(10, 0)`, which will always crash at runtime.\n\nRule from [`CLAUDE.md`](https://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/CLAUDE.md#L11): _\"Ensure inputs are validated to prevent runtime crashes like `ZeroDivisionError`.\"_\n\nAdd a guard:\n```python\ndef calculate(x, y):\n    if y == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"y must not be zero\")\n    return x / y\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/app_utils.py#L22-L25"
    },
    {
      "path": "app_utils.py",
      "line": 33,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**CLAUDE.md violation: Bare `except:` clause**\n\nA bare `except:` catches everything including `KeyboardInterrupt`, `SystemExit`, and `MemoryError`. Combined with `pass`, all exceptions are silently swallowed and failures become invisible.\n\nRule from [`CLAUDE.md`](https://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/CLAUDE.md#L10): _\"Do not use bare `except:` clauses. Always specify the exact Exception being caught and handle it properly.\"_\n\nSpecify the exception type and handle it:\n```python\n    except Exception as e:\n        logger.error(\"Failed to process users: %s\", e)\n        return []\n```\n\nhttps://github.com/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/blob/641eba3799c4ff48c41d744998b316f511c881d1/app_utils.py#L31-L35"
    }
  ]
}
ENDJSON
gh api repos/YCITC/reuse-workflow-test/pulls/12/reviews --method POST --input /tmp/pr_review.json', 'description': 'Post PR review with 6 inline comments via JSON file'})

